el et al. (2015) as the authentic environmental entry point to C3 nitrogen skeleton for cyanosulfidic networks.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_002\",\n      \"name\": \"Nucleophilic addition of NH3: acrylonitrile \u2192 \u03b2-aminopropionitrile\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_003\", \"mol_004\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_005\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-310K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"pH ~8\u20139, can occur in environmental pools\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Direct addition of ammonia to acrylonitrile across the double bond forms \u03b2-aminopropionitrile.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Explicitly demonstrated in Patel et al. (2015); efficient nucleophilic addition.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_003\",\n      \"name\": \"Photoreduction: \u03b2-aminopropionitrile \u2192 \u03b2-aminopropionaldehyde\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_010\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_006\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [\"UV light\", \"H2S\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-310K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"Requires strong UV (\u03bb<260nm), millimolar H2S\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"H2S-driven, UV-catalyzed photoreduction of the nitrile group to aldehyde.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Central photochemical step from Patel et al. (2015). Supported for shallow, UV-exposed aqueous pools (Ranjan et al. 2018).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_004\",\n      \"name\": \"Guanidination: \u03b2-aminopropionaldehyde + cyanamide \u2192 guanidinated hemiaminal\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_006\", \"mol_007\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_008\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \