m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: Arginine\nOVERALL STRATEGY: Network construction integrates all experimentally supported, chemically justified routes to prebiotic arginine, respecting contested evidence and distinguishing high-confidence cyanosulfidic, ornithine-guanidination, protometabolic, heterogeneous-catalysis, and historical photochemical modules. The core cyanosulfidic (Patel et al.) pathway is detailed from HCN/acetylene through the explicit arginine \u03b1-aminonitrile, then hydrolyzed to arginine. Parallel, shorter ornithine guanidination routes (free or post-polymer) are included, as well as a low-confidence high-T catalysis route, and speculative metabolic extensions from glutamate. All pathways consider environmental/geochemical constraints and critique, with explicit cross-environment rationale where supported by evidence.\n\nMOLECULES (23 nodes):\n  - mol_001: HCN (hydrogen cyanide) [starting]\n  - mol_002: C2H2 (acetylene) [starting]\n  - mol_003: CH2=CH\u2013CN (acrylonitrile) [intermediate]\n  - mol_004: NH3 (ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_005: NH2CH2CH2CN (\u03b2-aminopropionitrile) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_006: NH2CH2CH2CHO (\u03b2-aminopropionaldehyde) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_007: CN2H2 (cyanamide) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_008: NH2CH2CH2C(=NH)NH