nmental_progression\": 0.9,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.65,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.66,\n            \"feedback\": \"Metabolism-like extension: the reductive amination of \u03b1-ketoglutarate to glutamate (rxn_012) is directly supported by recent experiments. The speculative nonenzymatic glutamate\u2192ornithine (rxn_011) step does not yet have compelling prebiotic evidence or mass conservation, making the pathway incomplete beyond glutamate. Guanidination step (rxn_010) is literature-supported but limited by Orn supply. Environment assignments fit experimental precedent.\",\n            \"approved\": false,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_011\"],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Expand support for the Glu\u2192Orn step or note explicitly it has only speculative status.\",\n                \"Clarify missing co-products needed for overall mass/charge balance.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P7\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_017\": 0.4,\n                \"rxn_016\": 0.3,\n                \"rxn_010\": 0.93\n            },\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.6,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.8,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.9,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.82,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.70,\n            \"feedback\": \"Hybrid pathway leveraging volcanic Orn synthesis and cyanosulfidic guanidination. Ornithine formation is still limited by atom/charge balance and yields; guanidination step is robust. Gathering both in one scenario is environmentally plausible but not yet experimentally confirmed.\",\n            \"approved\": false,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_017\", \"rxn_016\"],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Resolve conservation for Orn synthesis.\",\n                \"Cite quantitative environmental pathway convergence where available.\"\n            ]\n