rn residue reacts with cyanamide to install guanidino (Arg) side chain.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Direct and complete Orn\u2192Arg conversion by cyanamide shown in model peptides by Longo et al. (2020, PNAS).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_013\",\n      \"name\": \"Reductive amination of \u03b1-ketoglutarate to glutamate\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_021\", \"mol_018\", \"mol_019\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_022\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Hydrothermal\",\n      \"agents\": [\"Ni/SiO2-Al2O3 (or meteoritic Ni)\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"295\u2013320K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1\u20135 bar H2\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"nickel or meteoritic minerals\",\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"pH 8, moderate Ni loading\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Ni-catalyzed reductive amination: NH3 and H2 reduce the ketone to an amine.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Directly and efficiently demonstrated by Kaur et al. (2024, Chem).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_014\",\n      \"name\": \"Speculative nonenzymatic conversion: glutamate \u2192 ornithine\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_022\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_014\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Hydrothermal\",\n      \"agents\": [\"Fe2+ mineral \u2013 speculative\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300\u2013320K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 bar\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"ferrous iron minerals (speculative)\",\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"possible step in rTCA or nonenzymatic metabolism\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Speculative displace/decarboxylate and aminate to produce Orn from Glu.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"No direct experimental support; included as logical prebiotic extension (see Kaur et al., 2024, for current limit). Atom conserved except for loss of CO2 (not shown as product per schema guidelines).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_015\",\n      \"name\": \"Fischer\u2013Tropsch-type (FTT) surface-catalyzed,