ous": true, "other": "mildly alkaline, presence of UV"}, "mechanism": "Copper(I) catalyzes oxidative coupling between acetylene and HCN, forming acrylonitrile.", "reasoning": "Supported by Patel et al. (2015), which demonstrates this key entry step in the cyanosulfidic network."}, {"id": "rxn_002", "name": "Nucleophilic addition of ammonia to acrylonitrile (Strecker-type)", "inputs": ["mol_004", "mol_005"], "outputs": ["mol_006"], "environment": "Surface", "agents": [null], "conditions": {"temperature": "300\u2013320K", "pressure": "1 atm", "catalyst": null, "aqueous": true, "other": "neutral or mildly alkaline conditions"}, "mechanism": "Ammonia attacks acrylonitrile's nitrile group, yielding \u03b2-aminopropionitrile.", "reasoning": "Direct step shown in Patel et al. (2015) and classic Strecker aminonitrile formation."}, {"id": "rxn_003", "name": "H2S/UV photoreduction of \u03b2-aminopropionitrile to \u03b2-aminopropionaldehyde", "inputs": ["mol_006", "mol_007"], "outputs": ["mol_008"], "environment": "Surface", "agents": ["UV light"], "conditions": {"temperature": "300\u2013320K", "pressure": "1 atm", "catalyst": "UV light, H2S (photoreductant)", "aqueous": true, "other": "UV irradiation (254 nm typical), sufficient sulfide"}, "mechanism": "Nitrile undergoes photoreduction in H2S/UV system to aldehyde.", "reasoning": "Patel et al. (2015) provides direct mechanistic and experimental evidence for H2S/UV-driven reduction of aminonitriles."}, {"id": "rxn_004", "name": "Cyanamide guanidination of \u03b2-aminopropionaldehyde", "inputs": ["mol_008", "mol_009"], "outputs": ["mol_010"], "environment": "Surface", "agents": [null], "conditions": {"temperature": "300\u2013320K", "pressure": "1 atm", "catalyst": null, "aqueous": true, "other": "neutral, prompt addition of cyanamide after photoreduction"}, "mechanism": "Imine/amine of \u03b2-aminopropionaldehyde attacks cyanamide, producing a guanidinated hemiaminal.", "reasoning": "Key enhanced-yield step in Patel et al. (201